{"id": "EUVD-2026-96699", "enisaUuid": "4bf7a4ff-659a-3458-a92a-21f02c054f61", "description": "CoreShop through 1.5.5 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in the OrderController that allows authenticated customers to act on other customers' orders by supplying user-controlled ids. Attackers can omit the data field in OrderConfirm or supply another reshipId to SendReship to confirm receipt of others' orders and overwrite return tracking details.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T01:35:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T12:58:29", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/SkVjopPsGe", "https://github.com/CoreUnion/CoreShop/blob/ca7408b025bc5f3fd5957a79618ffe991c4e91ab/CoreCms.Net.Web.WebApi/Controllers/OrderController.cs#L281-L294", "https://github.com/CoreUnion/CoreShop/blob/ca7408b025bc5f3fd5957a79618ffe991c4e91ab/CoreCms.Net.Web.WebApi/Controllers/OrderController.cs#L422-L458", "https://github.com/CoreUnion/CoreShop/blob/ca7408b025bc5f3fd5957a79618ffe991c4e91ab/CoreCms.Net.Services/Order/CoreCmsOrderServices.cs#L2048-L2060", "https://github.com/CoreUnion/CoreShop", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/coreshop-through-1.5.5-authorization-bypass-via-ordercontroller-orderconfirm-and-sendreship"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108696", "GHSA-7jj7-hfg8-m26w"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "acd31782-7c81-323f-be9d-73a87ccc00e8", "product": {"name": "CoreShop", "vendor": {"name": "coreshop"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.5.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7048f1c1-c405-3f9b-9537-dc2f5d41d8e2", "vendor": {"name": "CoreUnion"}}], "isExploited": false}